<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Phase 8b's gated GPU spike, and nothing else.

    The plan's question is narrow and answerable before any provider-pack,
    portable-folder or fallback work is designed: FIRST AUDIO is ~750 ms of which
    ~600 ms is the model's fixed cost for one inference (Phase 3), so the gate —
    30% off first-audio latency, no RTF regression, clean fall back to CPU — is
    really "does a GPU win on a single small inference, including everything it
    costs to get there". That is the least favourable shape for a GPU and the
    most favourable for a decision.

    NOT a backend project. The plan says the GPU backend gets built only if the
    gate passes, so building it first would be committing to the answer before
    measuring it — the exact move Phase 0 was structured to avoid. (The gate
    passed, and what it turned into is in the port plan's 8b record; this
    remains the thing that measured it, and is how the question gets re-asked on
    other hardware.)

    Why it references no backend project: at the time this was written the
    backend pinned the CPU-only Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime, and the GPU package
    publishes the same managed assembly name. Two packages, one assembly name,
    one output directory — the later copy wins silently. So this compiles
    SupertonicSdk.cs itself, and keeps its own answer independent of whatever the
    product currently links.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <AssemblyName>vst-gpu-spike</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>VibeSuperTonic.Spike.GpuCuda</RootNamespace>
    <RuntimeIdentifiers>linux-x64</RuntimeIdentifiers>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      The Linux GPU package: onnxruntime_providers_cuda.so plus the shared
      provider bridge. It does NOT carry CUDA or cuDNN — those are the
      gigabytes the plan says cannot ride in the default download, and this
      spike finds them through LD_LIBRARY_PATH rather than pretending otherwise.
      Version-matched to the CPU package (see the pin warning in the Engine).
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime.Gpu.Linux" Version="1.22.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\VibeSuperTonic.Core\VibeSuperTonic.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="..\..\src\VibeSuperTonic.Engine\Synth\SupertonicSdk.cs" Link="Shared\SupertonicSdk.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
